sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant D as Terminal at the site
    participant E as Tenant-scoped ingest edge
    participant A as Vendor adapter, versioned
    participant S as Punch store and quarantine
    participant X as Exception worklist

    D->>E: handshake with serial and per-device secret
    E->>E: resolve the route token to exactly one tenant, before any parsing
    alt serial unregistered or secret wrong
        E-->>D: rejected, timing identical to an unknown route
        E->>X: security event, nothing ingested in any tenant
    else admitted
        E-->>D: accepted, adapter version pinned for this session
    end

    D->>E: attendance-log upload, buffered burst after reconnect
    E->>E: size cap and per-device rate cap checked
    alt payload above the size cap or device throttled
        E-->>D: rejected with the vendor retry semantics preserved
        Note over D: the device keeps its buffer, so no punch is lost
    else within caps
        E->>S: raw bytes and payload hash written durably first
        E->>A: parse
        A->>S: normalised punch rows, deduplicated on the ingest key
        S-->>E: durable
        E-->>D: acknowledge only what is durable
    end

    A->>S: unparseable records to quarantine with their raw bytes
    S->>X: one item per device and adapter version, never one per record
    Note over A,S: a template or image on an attendance record is stripped before persistence
